---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NavBar from '../components/NavBar.astro';
import Diagram from '../components/Diagram.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Benchmarks" description="amber benchmark results: harness KPI progression and multi-model evaluation across 49 scenarios.">
  <NavBar />
  <main>
    <h1>Benchmarks</h1>

    <section class="section">
      <p>
        amber-bench is the KPI harness, how well the agent loop, tool schemas,
        and prompts drive each model to the correct solution. This is a harness
        score, not a model leaderboard: every scenario runs through the same
        engine, and the score measures the harness+model pair.
      </p>
      <p>
        The benchmark corpus has grown over time. The current dataset is 49
        scenarios across 10 suites (agent failures, terminal work, tool
        selection, prompt adherence, coding, refactoring, repo, review,
        delegate, and the loop-live axis measuring model loop discipline).
      </p>
      <p>
        Scoring: each scenario earns 0-100 from four sub-scores, correctness
        (bullseye + hidden-test artifact), efficiency (steps/wasted/redundant
        vs expected), robustness (retries/recoveries/hard-stops), and
        adherence (prompt-checks minus forbidden-tool use). The model score is
        the difficulty-weighted aggregate (1-5 per scenario), scaled to /1000.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider-thick" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Harness progression</h2>
      <p>
        The benchmark exists to measure the harness itself, to track how
        architecture changes move the KPIs. These are the recorded baselines
        for the Qwopus3.6-27B model as the engine evolved:
      </p>
      <table class="bench-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Baseline</th>
            <th>Date</th>
            <th>Scenarios</th>
            <th>Score</th>
            <th>Pass</th>
            <th>Change</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>v2 (first live calibration)</td>
            <td>2026-08-11</td>
            <td>43</td>
            <td>769.1</td>
            <td>39/43</td>
            <td>-</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>v3 (post-fix run)</td>
            <td>2026-08-12</td>
            <td>43</td>
            <td><strong>821.6</strong></td>
            <td>41/43</td>
            <td>+52.5 pts, +2 scenarios</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>v4 (loop-live axis added)</td>
            <td>2026-08-12</td>
            <td>49</td>
            <td>788.2</td>
            <td>42/49</td>
            <td>new axis, not comparable</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        The v2→v3 jump (+52.5 points) came from oracle path normalization,
        bare-JSON extraction, and an SSE-sink lifetime fix, all harness
        defects the benchmark itself surfaced. The v4 run added the loop-live
        suite (6 scenarios measuring plan design, adherence, repeat
        discipline, termination, tool choice, output interpretation), so its
        score is not directly comparable to v3.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Model population (2026-08-13)</h2>
      <p>
        All 10 models in the local swap registry, benchmarked live on the
        fixed harness (49 scenarios each, serial execution, single GPU slot).
        Records: <code>bench/results/&lt;alias&gt;-bench.json</code>. Harness
        floor: <code>bench/results/harness-baseline-v2.json</code> (42/42
        probes, integrity 1.0).
      </p>
      <table class="bench-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Model</th>
            <th>Score</th>
            <th>Pass</th>
            <th>Loop-live</th>
            <th>Wasted</th>
            <th>Redundant</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Qwen3.6-27B (dense)</td>
            <td><strong>816.2</strong></td>
            <td>44/49</td>
            <td>89.0</td>
            <td>146</td>
            <td>12</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Qwopus3.6-27B-v2-MTP</td>
            <td>808.0</td>
            <td>42/49</td>
            <td>76.2</td>
            <td>142</td>
            <td>12</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Gemma-4-31B</td>
            <td>806.2</td>
            <td>38/49</td>
            <td>75.9</td>
            <td>108</td>
            <td>8</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Gemma-4-12B Q4</td>
            <td>780.0</td>
            <td>37/49</td>
            <td>75.8</td>
            <td>120</td>
            <td>17</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Ornith-1.0-35B</td>
            <td>770.0</td>
            <td>40/49</td>
            <td>75.6</td>
            <td>192</td>
            <td>43</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Qwen3.6-27B MTP</td>
            <td>768.8</td>
            <td>41/49</td>
            <td>77.1</td>
            <td>166</td>
            <td>17</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Gemma-4-12B Q8</td>
            <td>756.8</td>
            <td>37/49</td>
            <td>75.8</td>
            <td>135</td>
            <td>28</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (MoE)</td>
            <td>742.2</td>
            <td>36/49</td>
            <td>65.9</td>
            <td>183</td>
            <td>36</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Qwen3.6-27B (pi-reasoning)</td>
