        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Key findings</h2>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>Dense 27B leads</strong>: the Qwen3.6-27B dense variants (816/808) are the strongest local agentic models, the 27B dense family is consistently at the top.</li>
        <li><strong>MoE costs tool discipline</strong>: the 35B MoE (742) and pi-reasoning (723) trail despite size, MoE routing and reasoning modes cost tool discipline.</li>
        <li><strong>Tool economy varies widely</strong>: Gemma-4-31B has the best tool economy (108 wasted, 8 redundant) but fails more scenario checks (38/49); Ornith-9B collapses on loop discipline (271 wasted, 122 redundant).</li>
        <li><strong>The benchmark catches harness bugs</strong>: the v2 calibration run surfaced three harness defects (oracle normalization, JSON extraction, SSE-sink lifetime), all fixed, the +52.5 point v2→v3 jump is the result.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Scenario suites</h2>
      <p>49 scenarios across 10 suites:</p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>Coding (5)</strong>: fizzbuzz, sorting, ring buffer, LCS, graph BFS</li>
        <li><strong>Prompt adherence (5)</strong>: envelope format, banned tool refusal, verify-after-action, multi-constraint, verify-before-claim</li>
        <li><strong>Refactoring (4)</strong>: extract method, polymorphism-over-switch, adapter, strategy</li>
        <li><strong>Terminal work (6)</strong>: ls count files, grep extract value, compile run cpp, env inventory, pipeline transform, multi-dir count</li>
        <li><strong>Tool selection (6)</strong>: search vs bash grep, read vs cat, write vs rewrite, process vs blocking, write-verify-loop</li>
        <li><strong>Agent failures (6)</strong>: redundant call elimination, mistake-then-recover, mid-stream dropout, parallel vs sequential, empty-reply recovery, tool-denied grace</li>
        <li><strong>Loop-live (6)</strong>: loop termination, output interpretation, plan adherence, plan design, loop repeat, tool choice</li>
        <li><strong>Repo (2)</strong>: repository navigation and search</li>
        <li><strong>Review (8)</strong>: arch, clean, datastructures, patterns, quality, refactor, code review perception scenarios</li>
        <li><strong>Delegate (1)</strong>: sub-agent delegation</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Reproducing</h2>
      <div class="terminal">
        <pre># Hermetic mode (no model needed, fake LLM, deterministic, CI-safe)
./amber-bench run

# Live mode (requires a running OpenAI-compatible server)
./amber-bench run --live --profile qwopus-27b --out results/qwopus-27b.json
./amber-bench run --live --profile qwen35-dense --out results/qwen35-dense.json
./amber-bench report results/*.json --format markdown</pre>
      </div>
      <p>
        <Diagram
        name="benchHarness"
      />
      Raw per-run JSON lives in <code>bench/results/</code>. The full KPI
        record, methodology, and per-model scorecards are in
        <a href="https://github.com/jtrefon/amber/blob/main/BENCHMARK.md">BENCHMARK.md</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
